From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0151: blueline GPU: interrupts, recovery, DCVS, cache clean
 option (bluegpu=8)

On top of 0147. Only bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c.

Interrupts: GIC SPI 300 (INTID 332, level) through 0121's
sweet_spi_attach. The fence tail gets a second CACHE_FLUSH_TS with the
IRQ bit after its MEM_WRITE (a6xx_submit), writing seq to CP+0x2820; the
vsync thread sleeps on it in 2 ms slices instead of delay(50) polling.
Checked at bring-up with a fenced no-op; no interrupt -> polled as 0147.
RBBM_INT_0 error bits snapshot CP state in the handler (CP_INTERRUPT_
STATUS, SQE_STAT opcode, HW_FAULT, PROTECT_STATUS, IB1/IB2, cb0 FSR/FAR)
and are decoded once on the thread. A storm (> 20000/s) masks the line.
GMU "gmu" (305) and "hfi" (304) SPIs: watchdog bite, fence error, AHB
error, CM3 fault, logged; a bite or CM3 fault ends GPU presents.

Hang and recovery: RBBM hang detect (masked in the handler, as
a6xx_fault_detect_irq) or the bluegpu_present_hang_ms guard -> dump once
(CP state, 32 ring dwords around rptr, GX), SQE and VBIF halt, RBBM soft
reset, hw_init, SQE/RB registers, ME_INIT, CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 (or
SECVID_TRUST_CNTL 0), 0138's 2D setup, cb0 TLBI, fenced no-op; the hung
frame is a CPU copy and presents resume. bluegpu_recover_max (3) in a
minute, a failed step or a GMU fault: 0147's "present hang" (CPU
presents for the boot). bluegpu_test_hang=N (kind 1 IB to an unmapped
VA, 2 WAIT_REG_MEM forever, 3 garbage header; _every=S repeats).

Clock: bluegpu_mhz=N picks the lowest level >= N. bluegpu_dcvs=1: busy
% per >= 100 ms (GMU power counter 0 XOCLK, blit CP_ALWAYS_ON time as a
fallback) -> the lowest level running it at bluegpu_dcvs_target % (65),
up at once, down after 3 windows, legacy GMU DCVS OOB; the DDR vote
follows the level's peak bandwidth (bluegpu_bw_kbps=N fixes it).
Measured clock (CP ALWAYS_COUNT vs CP_ALWAYS_ON) logged per change.

Cache clean: bluegpu_present_clean=1 (default) DC CVAC as 0147; 0 none
(UNSAFE, test only); 2 a coherence probe at up (lines this CPU left
dirty, read by CP_MEM_TO_MEM through a WB inner-shareable mapping):
coherent -> surface slots mapped cacheable and no clean; the
first-present self-check short of PASS turns cleaning back on.
---
 bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c | 1111 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 1048 insertions(+), 63 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c b/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c
--- a/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c
@@ -328,6 +328,38 @@
  *  time per present, GPU blit time and submit-to-done (CP_ALWAYS_ON).
  *  bluegpu_present=0: resident, CPU presents (bring-up test only).
  *
+ * Interrupts, recovery, DCVS, cache clean option (0151, bluegpu=8):
+ *  - GIC SPI 300 (INTID 332, level; 0121's sweet_spi_attach) for RBBM_INT_0
+ *    (A6XX_INT_MASK). Each fence tail gets a CACHE_FLUSH_TS with the IRQ bit
+ *    after its MEM_WRITE; the vsync thread sleeps on it (2 ms slices) instead
+ *    of polling. Checked with a fenced no-op at bring-up; no interrupt ->
+ *    polling as 0147. Error bits snapshot CP state in the handler and are
+ *    decoded once on the thread (a6xx_cp_hw_err_irq). > 20000 interrupts in
+ *    a second: masked at the GIC. bluegpu_irq=0: polled.
+ *  - GMU SPIs 305 "gmu" (AO_HOST_INT: watchdog bite, fence error, AHB error)
+ *    and 304 "hfi" (CM3_FAULT only): logged; a bite or CM3 fault ends GPU
+ *    presents (no GMU restart here). bluegpu_gmu_irq=0: not attached.
+ *  - Hang = RBBM hang detect interrupt (hw_init's HANG_INT_CNTL) or the
+ *    bluegpu_present_hang_ms guard. Recovery (bluegpu_recover=1): dump once,
+ *    SQE + VBIF halt, RBBM soft reset, hw_init, SQE/RB registers, ME_INIT,
+ *    secure mode off as the zap left it, 0138's 2D setup, cb0 TLBI, fenced
+ *    no-op; the hung frame is a CPU copy. bluegpu_recover_max (3) in a
+ *    minute -> CPU presents for the boot (0147's "present hang").
+ *  - bluegpu_test_hang=N: a bad packet (bluegpu_test_hang_kind 1 IB to an
+ *    unmapped VA, 2 WAIT_REG_MEM forever, 3 garbage header) in front of the
+ *    first present N s after up; bluegpu_test_hang_every=S repeats it.
+ *  - bluegpu_mhz=N: the lowest level >= N (257 342 414 520 596 675 710) at
+ *    start. bluegpu_dcvs=1: every >= 100 ms of presents, busy % (GMU power
+ *    counter 0 XOCLK, else blit time) -> lowest level that runs it at
+ *    bluegpu_dcvs_target % (65) within bluegpu_dcvs_min..max; up at once,
+ *    down after 3 windows; legacy GMU DCVS OOB (a6xx_gmu_set_freq), the DDR
+ *    vote follows the level (bluegpu_bw_kbps=N fixes it). Logged per change.
+ *  - bluegpu_present_clean: 1 (default) DC CVAC to PoC per present; 0 no
+ *    clean (UNSAFE, measures what it costs); 2 a coherence probe at up
+ *    (CPU-dirty lines read by the CP through a cacheable inner-shareable
+ *    mapping): coherent -> surface slots mapped cacheable and no clean, else
+ *    the clean stays; a first-present self-check short of PASS reverts.
+ *
  * Sources (copies and SHAs in pixel3-ios-gpu/ref):
  *  - Linux 20eef29b: sdm845.dtsi (gpu@5000000, gmu@506a000 "gmu" 0x30000,
  *    gpucc@5090000, adreno_smmu@5040000), gpucc-sdm845.c (gmu_clk_src RCG
@@ -422,6 +454,7 @@
